course: dictionary
lesson: 14593
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word plucked is one of them. The words around it give you the clues, so read the whole sentence before you decide what it means. «Mia plucked a ripe apple from the tree.» Here plucked means picked with the fingers.
explain: «The chicken was plucked before it went into the oven.» Here plucked means the feathers had been pulled out. The same word has a different job. The clue is the chicken, not the fingers.
explain: «Sam plucked the strings of his guitar.» Here plucked means played by pulling and letting go of the strings. Guitars, harps and ukuleles are plucked instruments. Violins and cellos are bowed, so they are played with a bow instead.
explain: «Lily plucked up courage and spoke in class.» Here plucked up courage means she made herself brave, even though she felt nervous. You cannot pull courage off a tree, so when a phrase does not make sense word by word, read the whole phrase for its meaning.
fact: Plucked is the past form of the verb pluck: pluck, plucks, plucked, plucking.
fact: «Plucked» means pulled off or picked with the fingers, as in plucked flowers or fruit.
fact: «Plucked» can mean having the feathers pulled out, as in a plucked chicken.
fact: «Plucked» can mean pulled quickly out of somewhere, as when a rescuer plucked people from the sea.
fact: «Plucked up courage» means made yourself brave, even when you feel nervous.
exercise: «Mia plucked a ripe strawberry from the bush.» What does plucked mean here? | Played on a guitar | *Picked with the fingers | Made brave | Cooked in a pan
exercise: «The harp was plucked softly by the musician.» How was the harp played? | Hit with a hammer | Rubbed with a cloth | Blown through a tube | *By pulling and letting go of the strings
exercise: «Lily plucked up courage and spoke in class.» What does plucked up courage mean? | Ran out of the room | *Made herself brave | Lost her bag | Pulled hairs out of her head
test: «The rescuer plucked the boy from the flood.» What does plucked mean here? | Sang loudly | Painted red | Hit gently | *Pulled quickly out of somewhere
test: Which word is the past form of pluck? | plucks | *plucked | plucking | pluck
exam: Why can plucked mean brave in one sentence and picked fruit in another? | *Because the words around it give the clues to its meaning | Because it is a spelling mistake | Because it has no context at all | Because all words have only one meaning
